    "created_at": "2017-05-15T21:23:31Z",
    "updated_at": "2017-05-15T21:23:31Z",
    "body": "(Note: there are some issues around testing document.open() in live-dom-viewer, I believe because it uses document.open() to do its work.)\r\n\r\nIt looks like it's a 2/2 split, with Chrome/Safari actually calling window.open(). See https://w3c-test.org/html/dom/dynamic-markup-insertion/opening-the-input-stream/document.open-02.html, which tests that it does *not* call window.open().\r\n\r\nSo I guess we can change it to the more reasonable behavior, but let's be sure to file bugs. I think that will also moves this change out of the \"editorial\" realm, as previously the spec could really be interpreted either way (and apparently was).",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
